OL,3,GNEWSAHome of oldest restaurant given to
OL,4,ANational Trust
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe home of London's oldest restaurant,
OL,7,Fwhich has hosted famous faces from
OL,8,FCharles Dickens to Madonna over the
OL,9,Fpast two centuries, has been given to
OL,10,Fthe National Trust.
OL,12,FRules originally opened in 1798 at
OL,13,F34-35 Maiden Lane in Covent Garden and
OL,14,Fhas outlasted empires, survived the
OL,15,FBlitz and fought off development plans.
OL,17,FThe #11m freehold gift of the
OL,18,Frestaurant building along with its
OL,19,Fhistoric collection such as visitor
OL,20,Fbooks, menus, and photographs will now
OL,21,Fbe protected for future generations,
OL,22,Fthe National Trust said.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,326,320,200,140,0,100
